# Arguments passed to the tierd daemon (word-split by systemd).
#
# The node joins through the seeds compiled into the binary, so no seed argument
# is required; membership is then learned via gossip.
#
# Default (join via the built-in seeds):
TIER_ARGS=run 7777
#
# An explicit seed can be added and is dialed in addition (IPv4/IPv6 literal,
# port as a separate token):
#   TIER_ARGS=run 7777 203.0.113.10 7777
#   TIER_ARGS=run 7777 2001:db8::10 7777
#
# The daemon binds the IPv6 wildcard (dual-stack), so it listens on both IPv6
# and IPv4 at the given port.
